---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '9 June 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Travel Old Hollywood handles your data: analytics, affiliate links, third parties, and your rights under UK data-protection law."
>
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-[#fdfbf2] text-[#1a2b4c] p-4 md:p-12 font-sans" style="background-image: url('https://www.transparenttextures.com/patterns/aged-paper.png')">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto border-[12px] border-double border-[#1a2b4c] p-6 md:p-16 bg-[#fdfbf2] shadow-2xl relative">

      <Header backLink="/" backLabel="Return to Lobby" variant="light" />

      <div class="text-center mb-12 mt-8">
        <p class="font-oswald uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-sm mb-4 text-[#8b5a2b]">The Small Print</p>
        <h1 class="font-anton text-4xl md:text-6xl tracking-wide uppercase mb-4 text-[#1a2b4c]">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-4">
          <div class="h-px w-12 bg-[#1a2b4c]"></div>
          <span class="font-typewriter text-sm text-[#8b5a2b]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
          <div class="h-px w-12 bg-[#1a2b4c]"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8 font-sans text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#2b3a55] [&_h2]:font-serif [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:md:text-3xl [&_h2]:text-[#1a2b4c] [&_h2]:mt-2 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_a]:text-[#c13a3a] [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-2 hover:[&_a]:text-[#1a2b4c] [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:space-y-2 [&_li]:marker:text-[#d4b872]">

        <section>
          <p>
            Travel Old Hollywood ("we", "us") is a travel publication at traveloldhollywood.com, operated as
            a sole trader in the United Kingdom and the data controller responsible for this site. This policy
            explains what information is collected when you visit, how it is used, and the rights you have. We
            aim to collect as little as possible. You can reach us any time at
            <a href="mailto:adam@vintagetravel.co.uk">adam@vintagetravel.co.uk</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <p>
            We don't ask you to create an account, we don't run a newsletter or collect your details through
            forms, and we don't sell your data to anyone. We use privacy-friendly, aggregate analytics to see
            how the site performs, and some of our outbound links are affiliate links that set their own
            cookies if you click them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Information we collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Aggregate analytics.</strong> We use Vercel Web Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights to
              understand, in aggregate, how the site is used and how quickly pages load. These are designed to
              be privacy-friendly: they do not use cookies to track visitors and do not build an advertising
              profile of you.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Affiliate-link data.</strong> When you click an affiliate link, the partner you're sent
              to (for example a hotel-booking platform or retailer) may set cookies or use similar technology
              to credit us if you go on to book or buy. That data is collected and controlled by them, under
              their own privacy policies — see "Third parties" below. Our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a>
              explains the commercial side.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Standard server logs.</strong> Like virtually all websites, our hosting provider
              automatically records technical information such as IP address, browser type and the pages
              requested, for security and to keep the service running.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            We do not set our own marketing or tracking cookies. Our analytics are cookieless. The main cookies
            you may encounter come from third-party affiliate partners, and only if you click one of their
            links. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time without affecting your
            ability to read the site.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third parties</h2>
          <p>We rely on a small number of trusted providers:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — website hosting and the aggregate analytics described above.</li>
            <li><strong>Affiliate partners and networks</strong> — such as Booking.com, Travelpayouts, GetYourGuide, Viator, DiscoverCars, Airalo, Amazon Associates and Awin — which may receive click and transaction data when you follow one of their links. Each operates under its own privacy policy.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Some of these providers are based outside the UK, including in the United States, so your data may be transferred and processed internationally under appropriate safeguards.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Under the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018 you have the right to access, correct, or ask us
            to delete personal data we hold about you, and to object to or restrict certain processing. As we
            don't operate accounts or collect contact details directly, we typically hold no personal data that
            identifies you. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:adam@vintagetravel.co.uk">adam@vintagetravel.co.uk</a>.
            If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, you can complain to the UK Information
            Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Children</h2>
          <p>This site is intended for a general adult audience and is not directed at children under 13.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy as the site evolves or our partners change. When we do, we'll revise the
            "last updated" date above. Material changes will be made clear on this page.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
